<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11710" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄπειμι</span></b>  (B), (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἶμι</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>ibo</i>), serving as
			fut. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπέρχομαι</span>:
				inf.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπιέναι,</span> in <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				11.404
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Lucill.
			</span></i>) <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπίναι</span>:—<i>go
				away, depart,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Od.
				17.593
			</span></i>, al.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἄπει;</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄπιθι</span>
			, <i>begone,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				431
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπιὼν οἴχεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					18.65
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				17.43
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ πρέσβεις περὶ τῶν σπονδῶν ἀπῇσαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					4.39
				</span></i>
			; of soldiers, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπίασι οὐδενὶ κόσμῳ</span>”
				<i>will retreat,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					8.60
				</span></i>
			.<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γ́; ἀ. πρὸς βασιλέα</span>
			<i>desert</i> to him, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				1.9.29
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. πάλιν</span>
			<i>return,</i> ib.<i><span class="en">
				1.4.7
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				15
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄπιτε ἐπὶ τὰ ὑμέτερα αὐτῶν</span>
			<i>return</i> to your homes, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				6.97
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄπιμεν οἴκαδε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>V.</u>
					255
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπῇσαν ἐπ᾽ οἴκου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					5.36
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς τὴν πατρίδα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arr.
					<u>Epict.</u>
					2.23.36
				</span></i>
			; of the Nile, <i>recede.</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.108
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἐπί τι</span>
			<i>go</i> in quest of . ., <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				7.5.80
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηνὸς ἀπιόντος,</span> for the
			common <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φθίνοντος,</span> Decr. ap. <i><span class="en">
				D.
				18.37
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>CIG</u>
				3658
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Cyzicus</span>); <i>die,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Tim.</u>
				15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>Im.</u>
				2.9
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c. acc.
			cogn., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολλὴν καὶ τραχεῖαν
			ἀπιέναι</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁδόν</span>)
				<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				272c
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>to be discharged,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Mul.</u>
				8
			</span></i>, al.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
